# Tor client config for the rsched `tor` service — SOCKS only, no relay, no exit.

# Listen on the container's network interface, not just loopback: the CLIENT is a different
# container (rsched), so 127.0.0.1 would be unreachable. This is safe only because the compose
# service publishes NO ports — the socket is reachable only from the compose network. Never add
# a `ports:` mapping for 9050; that would expose an open proxy to the LAN.
SocksPort 0.0.0.0:9050

# Belt to the no-published-ports brace: accept the RFC1918 ranges Docker assigns, refuse the rest.
SocksPolicy accept 10.0.0.0/8
SocksPolicy accept 172.16.0.0/12
SocksPolicy accept 192.168.0.0/16
SocksPolicy reject *

# Never carry traffic for anyone else.
ClientOnly 1
ExitRelay 0

DataDirectory /var/lib/tor
# stdout so `docker compose logs tor` shows bootstrap progress; notice level keeps it quiet
# once running. Tor logs no client request paths at this level.
Log notice stdout
